          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q. Can we make 1,000 using the numbers in the middle? Why not? What about 14,000, 15,000 and 16,000? Yes, it is possible. Explore how. What thousands cannot be made?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Ans. No; the only number which is smaller than 1000 is 400 and 1000 is not a multiple of 400."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.464,
            0.412,
            0.515
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_27_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}14000 &= 1500 \\times 8 + 400 \\times 5 \\\\&= 12000 + 2000 \\\\&= 14000\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.516,
            0.393,
            0.567
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_27_equation_13.jpg",
          "content": "{ \\begin{array} { r l } { 1 5 0 0 0 = 1 3 0 0 0 + 4 0 0 \\times 5 } \\\\ { = 1 3 0 0 0 + 2 0 0 0 } \\\\ { = 1 5 0 0 0 } \\end{array} }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.178,
            0.569,
            0.422,
            0.62
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_27_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}16000 &= 1500 \\times 8 + 400 \\times 10 \\\\&= 12000 + 4000 \\\\&= 16000\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.623,
            0.531,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Only one thousand (1000) cannot be made."
